        <OtherAbstract Type="PIP" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>55 patients, aged 18-40, for whom functional dysmenorrhea had been diagnosed, were inserted with the Progestasert, a progesterone-releasing IUD, on the 4th day of cycle. 14 patients had previously been treated with estroprogestinic agents for dysmenorrhea, but had stopped the treatment because of its side effects. All patients were checked 1, 6, and 12 months after insertion. Menstrual and premenstrual pain regressed sensibly after the first month, and almost disappeared after the 6th. A normalization of the menstrual cycle was also noted. No side effects were reported.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
